    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **48 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the soft-match (\"possible duplicate\") rule for owner creation. When a new owner isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` with a *different* telephone, it's still created and flagged.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added two read-only properties to the `Owner` schema: `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (int32 id). These generate the corresponding `OwnerDto` fields, which MapStruct maps by name automatically.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added `possibleDuplicate` (`Boolean`) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (`Integer`) persistent fields with `@Column` mappings and getters/setters.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 After the hard-duplicate (identityKey) check passes, it now computes the soft match and sets the flags before saving. Added a `findPossibleDuplicate` helper that returns the lowest-id existing owner sharing the normalized last name and the same postcode but with a different telephone (`null` if the new owner has no postcode or no match). Owners with the same telephone are excluded, since those fall under the hard-duplicate rule.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 Added `possible_duplicate` and `possible_duplicate_of` columns. The hsqldb one matters for tests (`ddl-auto=none`); the others keep the schemas consistent.\n\nThe new `Cp35Tests` passes (asserting `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf=ida`), the hard-duplicate `Cp10Tests` still rejects with 409, and no existing tests regressed. For fully-unique owners, `possibleDuplicate` is set to `false`, per the spec's \"otherwise false\".",
